  ('4d3568dc-27fa-5a9a-b761-f2d9fac1d4a2', 'en-ak8-mastare-verb', 'Engelska', 'ak8', 'Verb', 'Mästarprov: Verb', 'Blandade frågor ur hela området, i ny ordning varje gång. Klarar du det med minst två stjärnor sitter området.', 4, 'mastare', null, 'vag'),
  ('48c6f60e-3d58-51bb-928e-3862baa96c25', 'en-ak8-adjektiv-1', 'Engelska', 'ak8', 'Adjektiv', 'Bigger, better, best', 'Komparativ och superlativ med -er och -est, med more och most, och de oregelbundna.', 5, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('63dfce4e-0f41-5e99-83bc-cafbedc5071f', 'en-ak8-adjektiv-2', 'Engelska', 'ak8', 'Adjektiv', 'Quick or quickly?', 'Adjektiv och adverb: quick och quickly, good och well, bored och boring.', 6, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('1c888eaf-15e7-5f05-bd85-bc2f7cf00261', 'en-ak8-mastare-adjektiv', 'Engelska', 'ak8', 'Adjektiv', 'Mästarprov: Adjektiv', 'Blandade frågor ur hela området, i ny ordning varje gång. Klarar du det med minst två stjärnor sitter området.', 7, 'mastare', null, 'vag'),
  ('7b88e6b8-e1d2-5444-9924-3908b5ed4c7d', 'en-ak8-prepositioner-1', 'Engelska', 'ak8', 'Prepositioner', 'In, on eller at?', 'In, on och at för tid och plats, och ordföljden kring dem.', 8, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('83af83fa-6dc0-5457-963a-a2bae6948578', 'en-ak8-prepositioner-2', 'Engelska', 'ak8', 'Prepositioner', 'Afraid of, good at', 'Prepositioner som hör ihop med vissa verb och adjektiv.', 9, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('348fef6d-036a-5664-b850-64f3d70b3bbd', 'en-ak8-mastare-prepositioner', 'Engelska', 'ak8', 'Prepositioner', 'Mästarprov: Prepositioner', 'Blandade frågor ur hela området, i ny ordning varje gång. Klarar du det med minst två stjärnor sitter området.', 10, 'mastare', null, 'vag'),
  ('53b5b5e0-de8d-5a33-978f-62c972ea58b6', 'en-ak8-lasforstaelse-1', 'Engelska', 'ak8', 'Läsförståelse', 'The last bus', 'En berättelse på engelska om en kväll då Maya missar sista bussen, med frågor om vad som står och vad man kan förstå mellan raderna.', 11, 'vanlig', 'Maya missed the last bus by one minute. She stood at the empty stop and watched its red lights disappear around the corner. It was her own fault. Her mum had told her to leave the party at ten, and it was now twenty past.

Her phone was almost dead. She sent a quick message to her mum: “Missed the bus. Walking home.” Then the screen went black.

The walk would take forty minutes. Maya pulled up her hood and started along the main road, where the street lights were bright and a few cars still passed. The shortcut through the park would save fifteen minutes, but she had promised never to take it after dark.

Halfway home, a car slowed down beside her. Maya''s heart jumped. Then she saw the dented door and the sticker of a smiling sun on the back window. It was her mum''s car.

“Get in,” her mum said. Her voice was calm, but she was still wearing her slippers.

For a while neither of them spoke. Maya waited for the lecture: about being responsible, about charging her phone, about ten o''clock meaning ten o''clock.

Instead her mum said, “You didn''t go through the park.”

“How do you know?”

“Because I drove through it first.”

Maya looked down at the slippers and understood that her mum had not taken the time to change into shoes. She said sorry, and this time she really meant it.', 'vag'),
  ('432cf857-641e-5a9b-8849-d2043329ac9c', 'en-ak8-lasforstaelse-2', 'Engelska', 'ak8', 'Läsförståelse', 'The new neighbour', 'En berättelse om en ny granne som spelar piano, med frågor om vad som står och vad orden betyder.', 12, 'vanlig', 'When the moving van stopped outside number 14, the whole street was watching. For two years the house had been empty, and there were rumours about why: a ghost, a crime, a family that had left in the middle of the night.

The new neighbour turned out to be an old man with a white beard and a very large, very slow dog. He did not wave. He did not say hello. For the first week, the only sign of life was the dog, which lay on the front step all day like a rug.

Then the music started. Every evening at eight, piano music came through the open windows of number 14 – not simple tunes, but long, difficult pieces that went on for an hour. People stopped on the pavement to listen. Nobody knew what to think.

It was Jamal, who was eleven and not afraid of anything, who finally knocked on the door. He had a plate of his mother''s cinnamon buns as an excuse.

The old man opened the door, looked at the buns and then at Jamal. “You’re the boy who stands by my fence every evening,” he said.

Jamal went red. “I like the music,” he said.

“Then come in and hear it properly,” said the old man. “But leave your shoes by the door. The dog eats them.”

That was how Jamal started taking piano lessons, and how the street learned that the old man had once played in concert halls all over the world.', 'vag'),
  ('31bc4e37-a704-5759-85e4-47b2059f440c', 'en-ak8-blad-irregular-1', 'Engelska', 'ak8', 'Övningsblad: oregelbundna verb', 'Went, ate, bought', 'Sex vanliga oregelbundna verb i dåtid: go, eat, buy, think, write och take. Bygger på övningsbladet «Irregular verbs – past tense» i materialbanken.', 13, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('8bfdc47e-9f3d-59b6-80dd-45b084113a21', 'en-ak8-blad-irregular-2', 'Engelska', 'ak8', 'Övningsblad: oregelbundna verb', 'Yesterday we went', 'Oregelbundna verb i dåtid i hela meningar om något som har hänt. Bygger på övningsbladet «Irregular verbs – past tense» i materialbanken.', 14, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('7e22ace6-1cff-570f-a7d2-c9c82f6abcb0', 'en-ak8-mastare-ovningsblad-oregelbundna-verb', 'Engelska', 'ak8', 'Övningsblad: oregelbundna verb', 'Mästarprov: Övningsblad: oregelbundna verb', 'Blandade frågor ur hela området, i ny ordning varje gång. Klarar du det med minst två stjärnor sitter området.', 15, 'mastare', null, 'vag'),
  ('aad55190-0de2-5874-a7f8-cd7e0887d131', 'en-ak8-fler-relativ-1', 'Engelska', 'ak8', 'Relativa bisatser', 'Who, which, where', 'Who, which och where: att binda ihop meningar om personer, saker och platser.', 16, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('3c8fb39f-d400-5974-932e-6e6b5fc88477', 'en-ak8-fler-relativ-2', 'Engelska', 'ak8', 'Relativa bisatser', 'Whose, that och långa meningar', 'Whose för vem något tillhör, och när man får och inte får utelämna who och that.', 17, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('06a672a9-0147-5e43-be8a-a1bbe3b2bf85', 'en-ak8-mastare-relativa-bisatser', 'Engelska', 'ak8', 'Relativa bisatser', 'Mästarprov: Relativa bisatser', 'Blandade frågor ur hela området, i ny ordning varje gång. Klarar du det med minst två stjärnor sitter området.', 18, 'mastare', null, 'vag'),
  ('06f15d6c-a12a-5a10-9e8f-86a0aa0fd9be', 'en-ak8-fler-lasa-1', 'Engelska', 'ak8', 'Läsa och förstå', 'Hidden in the book', 'En berättelse om ett kuvert i en begagnad bok, med frågor om vad som står och vad man kan förstå av det.', 19, 'vanlig', 'Selma found the envelope between pages 112 and 113 of a second-hand book. She had bought the book at a market for twenty kronor, and she had only opened it to check that no pages were missing.

Inside the envelope was a photograph of two girls on a beach, laughing, with wet hair. On the back, someone had written in pencil: Dear Anna, never forget the summer of 1998. Love, Karin.

Selma looked at the photo for a long time. Somebody had kept this picture inside a book for more than twenty years, and then the book had ended up on a market table between a lamp and a box of old records.

Inside the cover there was a name and an address: Anna Berg, 4 Rose Street. Selma did not know if Anna still lived there. But the next Saturday she took the bus to Rose Street, rang the bell and held up the envelope. The woman who opened the door looked at it for a moment. Then she started to cry, and she asked Selma to come in for a cup of tea.', 'vag'),
  ('80a71075-aff6-5857-96d8-2930c1ccb0e7', 'en-ak8-fler-lasa-2', 'Engelska', 'ak8', 'Läsa och förstå', 'A later start', 'En nyhetsartikel om en skola som provar att börja lektionerna senare, med frågor om vad som står och vad som menas.', 20, 'vanlig', 'At Linden School, lessons used to start at eight o’clock. This autumn, the head teacher, Ms Dahl, decided to try a later start, at nine. The trial will last one term.

The idea came from research on teenagers and sleep. Many young people go to bed late but still have to get up early, and Ms Dahl noticed that a lot of pupils were yawning in the first lesson. “It is hard to learn when you are half asleep,” she says.

After six weeks, the school asked pupils and teachers what they thought. Most pupils said that they felt more awake in the mornings, and teachers reported that fewer pupils arrived late. However, there were problems too. Some parents leave for work before nine, so their children are alone at home for an hour. Others pointed out that the school day now ends at four, which makes it harder to find time for football practice.

Ms Dahl will listen carefully before she decides anything. “A good idea for most pupils can still be a bad idea for some,” she says.', 'vag'),
  ('450f64d9-b42c-5a12-90fd-d58fb7a494c4', 'en-ak8-gerund-1', 'Engelska', 'ak8', 'Gerund och infinitiv', 'Enjoy swimming, want to swim', 'När ett verb kommer efter ett annat: efter vissa verb står -ing (enjoy, finish), efter andra to (want, decide), och efter en preposition står alltid -ing.', 21, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('76cf6291-1906-575a-aaf8-ac036104068d', 'en-ak8-gerund-2', 'Engelska', 'ak8', 'Gerund och infinitiv', 'Stop talking or stop to talk?', 'Verb som kan följas av både -ing och to, ibland med olika betydelse (stop, remember, forget, try, mean), och -ing som subjekt först i meningen.', 22, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('ac8e9d19-7918-51bc-8555-35d700773875', 'en-ak8-mastare-gerund-och-infinitiv', 'Engelska', 'ak8', 'Gerund och infinitiv', 'Mästarprov: Gerund och infinitiv', 'Blandade frågor ur hela området, i ny ordning varje gång. Klarar du det med minst två stjärnor sitter området.', 23, 'mastare', null, 'vag'),
  ('5822e1d1-c015-5490-9b6b-32bfc1d4246f', 'en-ak8-fragetaggar-1', 'Engelska', 'ak8', 'Frågetaggar', 'It''s cold, isn''t it?', 'Frågesvansar, som eller hur på svenska: svansen tar hjälpverbet ur meningen, och en jakande mening får en nekande svans.', 24, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('aea7c1b2-c6ef-5971-b571-06103ab887d9', 'en-ak8-fragetaggar-2', 'Engelska', 'ak8', 'Frågetaggar', 'I''m late, aren''t I?', 'De knepiga svansarna: aren’t I, let’s … shall we, uppmaningar, there is, ord som nobody och never, och svansen efter ett verb i dåtid.', 25, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('37107ed0-189e-5c71-80bd-dcd2b01acc55', 'en-ak8-mastare-fragetaggar', 'Engelska', 'ak8', 'Frågetaggar', 'Mästarprov: Frågetaggar', 'Blandade frågor ur hela området, i ny ordning varje gång. Klarar du det med minst två stjärnor sitter området.', 26, 'mastare', null, 'vag'),
  ('8613d588-1ce7-582a-a8d2-6d02eed4cc4e', 'en-ak8-mejl-1', 'Engelska', 'ak8', 'Formella och informella mejl', 'Dear Ms Berg or Hi Sam?', 'Hur du börjar, skriver och avslutar ett mejl, till en kompis och till någon du inte känner, som en skola, ett hotell eller ett museum.', 27, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('3ad0b013-a13a-5028-8151-f432599036e7', 'en-ak8-mejl-2', 'Engelska', 'ak8', 'Formella och informella mejl', 'Two emails about a school trip', 'Två mejl som Ella skriver om samma klassresa, ett formellt till ett vandrarhem och ett vardagligt till en kompis, med frågor om vad som står och hur hon skriver.', 28, 'vanlig', 'EMAIL 1, to the youth hostel

Subject: Group booking, 18–20 May

Dear Sir or Madam,

I am writing on behalf of Class 8B at Ekbacka School in Sweden. Our class is planning a trip to Port Alder in May, and we would like to stay at your youth hostel from 18 to 20 May.

We are 24 pupils and two teachers. Could you please tell me whether you have enough beds for our group, and how much it would cost per night? We would also like to know if breakfast is included in the price.

Two of the pupils are allergic to nuts. I would be grateful if you could tell me whether your kitchen can make meals without nuts.

Thank you in advance for your help. I look forward to hearing from you.

Yours faithfully,

Ella Nordin, Class 8B, Ekbacka School

EMAIL 2, to Ella’s friend Sam

Subject: Guess what?!

Hi Sam,

Guess what? We’re coming to Port Alder in May! The whole class, can you believe it? I’ve just emailed the youth hostel by the harbour to ask if they’ve got room for us. Fingers crossed!

We’ll be there from the 18th to the 20th. Are you free on the 19th? It’d be so cool to finally meet you in real life. Maybe you could show me that café you’re always going on about, the one with the giant pancakes?

Oh, and I had to write the hostel email in my best formal English. Took me ages! Mr Holm, our teacher, said it was perfect, so I’m feeling pretty proud.

Write back soon! Ella

PS Don’t tell anyone, but I’m a bit nervous about speaking English for three whole days.', 'vag'),
