  ('51c03d3d-bb9a-51d0-8107-3f05d0f3abf0', 'en-ak7-prepositioner-1', 'Engelska', 'ak7', 'Pronomen och prepositioner', 'On Monday, for three years', 'In, on, at, for och since när man pratar om tid.', 8, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('8890d5dd-91bb-5d64-bc27-c913240fb3c1', 'en-ak7-mastare-pronomen-och-prepositioner', 'Engelska', 'ak7', 'Pronomen och prepositioner', 'Mästarprov: Pronomen och prepositioner', 'Blandade frågor ur hela området, i ny ordning varje gång. Klarar du det med minst två stjärnor sitter området.', 9, 'mastare', null, 'vag'),
  ('bb34d93f-9673-5fed-a5f7-67a5a29146e0', 'en-ak7-meningar-1', 'Engelska', 'ak7', 'Meningar', 'Always, never, often', 'Var always, never, often och usually står i meningen.', 10, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('f48777c0-96a4-5299-bef6-80baa86fe4bf', 'en-ak7-meningar-2', 'Engelska', 'ak7', 'Meningar', 'Did you? I didn''t.', 'Frågor och nekanden i preteritum med did.', 11, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('cf011b50-e628-5f58-939c-7ff6e4709dd0', 'en-ak7-mastare-meningar', 'Engelska', 'ak7', 'Meningar', 'Mästarprov: Meningar', 'Blandade frågor ur hela området, i ny ordning varje gång. Klarar du det med minst två stjärnor sitter området.', 12, 'mastare', null, 'vag'),
  ('923ae9a5-7410-589f-a9a8-f84543708d49', 'en-ak7-lasforstaelse-1', 'Engelska', 'ak7', 'Läsförståelse', 'The robot', 'En berättelse om en robottävling, med frågor om vad som står och hur personerna känner sig.', 13, 'vanlig', 'Omar and Nora had worked on their robot for six weeks. It was small, with four wheels and a camera on top, and it was supposed to follow a black line on the floor without any help.

The school competition started at ten on Saturday morning. Twelve teams were taking part. When it was their turn, Omar put the robot on the start line and Nora pressed the button. The robot rolled forward, followed the line for two metres – and then turned left and drove straight into the wall.

Some people laughed. Omar''s face went red. He wanted to pick up the robot and go home.

“Wait,” Nora said. “It’s the light.” The sun was shining through the big windows, and the camera could not see the line in the bright light.

They had twenty minutes before their second try. Nora found some tape, and Omar made a small roof out of cardboard to put over the camera.

On the second try, the robot followed the whole line and stopped exactly at the finish. They did not win – they came fourth – but the judges gave them a special prize for solving a problem under pressure.

“Next year,” Omar said, “we’re bringing a roof from the start.”', 'vag'),
  ('849224cd-c089-5b17-b341-23fe30a3771c', 'en-ak7-lasforstaelse-2', 'Engelska', 'ak7', 'Läsförståelse', 'Lake Camp', 'Ett brev från en lägerledare, med frågor om vad som gäller på lägret.', 14, 'vanlig', 'Dear parents and campers,

We are happy that you have signed up for Lake Camp this summer! Camp starts on 2 July at 3 pm and ends on 8 July at 11 am.

Here are a few things to remember:

Please bring a sleeping bag, a towel, rain clothes and shoes that can get wet. We spend a lot of time outdoors, whatever the weather.

Mobile phones are allowed, but they must stay in the cabins during activities. Campers may use their phones between 7 and 8 pm every evening.

Everyone must pass a swimming test on the first day before they can use the canoes. The test is 200 metres in the lake. Campers who do not pass can still swim close to the beach with a leader.

Do not bring sweets or snacks. Food in the cabins attracts mice!

If your child needs medicine, please give it to a leader when you arrive, together with a note.

See you soon!

Jonas, camp leader', 'vag'),
  ('dff5e1a7-436f-5b5f-9c5b-54862348af3f', 'en-ak7-blad-farm-1', 'Engelska', 'ak7', 'Läsa: övningsblad', 'The school trip', 'Läsförståelse: en skolutflykt till en gård, med frågor om detaljer och ord. Bygger på övningsbladet «Reading: The school trip» i materialbanken.', 15, 'vanlig', 'Last Friday, my class went on a school trip to a farm outside the city. We left school at eight o''clock and took the bus. It was raining when we arrived, so we all put on our rain jackets and boots. First, we met the farmer, Mrs Ward. She showed us the cows, the pigs and a very friendly horse called Max. Then we helped to feed the chickens and collect the eggs. I found five eggs! After lunch, we made butter from cream. It was hard work, but it tasted great on fresh bread. On the bus back to school, everyone was tired but happy. I want to go there again next year.', 'vag'),
  ('e6c84dd2-7a14-5fd1-bf77-ca288e827cdf', 'en-ak7-fler-modala-1', 'Engelska', 'ak7', 'Modala hjälpverb', 'Can, could, must', 'Can, could och must: vad man kan, kunde och måste, och vad man inte får.', 16, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('8363577e-5df7-52af-9d2c-9194d8db74b6', 'en-ak7-fler-modala-2', 'Engelska', 'ak7', 'Modala hjälpverb', 'Should, might, have to', 'Should, might och have to: råd, möjlighet och det man måste eller inte behöver.', 17, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('e4b3516d-eede-580d-8e9a-7b1f0e15fe46', 'en-ak7-mastare-modala-hjalpverb', 'Engelska', 'ak7', 'Modala hjälpverb', 'Mästarprov: Modala hjälpverb', 'Blandade frågor ur hela området, i ny ordning varje gång. Klarar du det med minst två stjärnor sitter området.', 18, 'mastare', null, 'vag'),
  ('7100a0c5-beaf-5ac6-86cd-2eb0bb327ad9', 'en-ak7-fler-lasa-1', 'Engelska', 'ak7', 'Läsa och förstå', 'My week without a phone', 'Ett blogginlägg om en vecka utan telefon, med frågor om vad som hände och vad det betyder.', 19, 'vanlig', 'Last week I tried something new: seven days without my phone. My little sister Lisa had said that I could not do it, and I wanted to prove her wrong.

On Monday I felt strange. I kept putting my hand in my pocket, but there was nothing there. On the bus I had to look out of the window, and I saw a man walking a tiny dog that was wearing a red coat. I would never have noticed that before.

On Wednesday my friend Erik and I met at the park. We played football instead of looking at videos, and we talked for two hours. On Friday I finished a book that I had started in the summer.

Was it easy? No. I missed my music, and I got lost twice because I had no map. But I slept better, and I felt calmer. Now I have my phone again, but I will not use it in the evenings. Lisa says I will fail. We will see.', 'vag'),
  ('ed8e270c-4df7-5556-bd86-70b0d502d16a', 'en-ak7-fler-lasa-2', 'Engelska', 'ak7', 'Läsa och förstå', 'Bees on the roof', 'En artikel om en tonåring som har bin på taket, med frågor om vad som står och varför.', 20, 'vanlig', 'Thirteen-year-old Tara Ahmed has an unusual hobby: she keeps bees. Her hives stand on the flat roof of the building where she lives, and a neighbour who is a beekeeper taught her the basics.

“People think bees are dangerous,” Tara says. “But they only sting when they are afraid. If you move slowly and stay calm, they leave you alone.” She wears a white suit and a hat with a net, and she uses smoke to keep the bees quiet while she works.

Last summer her bees made forty kilos of honey. Tara gave some to the neighbours and sold the rest at a school market. With the money, she bought a second hive.

Tara knows that bees are in trouble in many places. “They need flowers,” she says. So the people in her building have planted flowers on every balcony. “It looks nicer too,” says Tara.', 'vag'),
  ('f3c0d2c8-d4f4-5cc5-aa45-9e086dc67b4a', 'en-ak7-perfekt-1', 'Engelska', 'ak7', 'Present perfect', 'I have seen, she has been', 'Present perfect: have eller has och verbets tredje form, ever och never, och de vanligaste oregelbundna formerna.', 21, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('175b9371-6ccc-554d-8217-9388cc976c20', 'en-ak7-perfekt-2', 'Engelska', 'ak7', 'Present perfect', 'Saw eller have seen?', 'När det heter present perfect och när det heter past simple: yesterday och last summer, just, yet och since, gone och been.', 22, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('48604d39-38d6-5956-b783-8c8d1579ded4', 'en-ak7-mastare-present-perfect', 'Engelska', 'ak7', 'Present perfect', 'Mästarprov: Present perfect', 'Blandade frågor ur hela området, i ny ordning varje gång. Klarar du det med minst två stjärnor sitter området.', 23, 'mastare', null, 'vag'),
  ('95b82070-75f7-57bb-bc6b-6064089034cf', 'en-ak7-mangd-1', 'Engelska', 'ak7', 'Some, any, much och many', 'Some or any?', 'Some och any: när man säger some och när man säger any, och orden somebody, nothing och somewhere.', 24, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('29271413-952b-5799-a22c-efe87f710411', 'en-ak7-mangd-2', 'Engelska', 'ak7', 'Some, any, much och many', 'Much, many, a few, a little', 'Much och many, a few och a little, och ord som går att räkna på svenska men inte på engelska, som advice och homework.', 25, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('af65b378-d41e-5ef2-8349-30c2b390ff50', 'en-ak7-mastare-some-any-much-och-many', 'Engelska', 'ak7', 'Some, any, much och many', 'Mästarprov: Some, any, much och many', 'Blandade frågor ur hela området, i ny ordning varje gång. Klarar du det med minst två stjärnor sitter området.', 26, 'mastare', null, 'vag'),
  ('9fb91941-62d0-5e21-9eaa-6fc836398a55', 'en-ak7-brittiskt-amerikanskt-1', 'Engelska', 'ak7', 'Brittisk och amerikansk engelska', 'Flat or apartment?', 'Ord och stavning som skiljer brittisk och amerikansk engelska åt: flat och apartment, lift och elevator, colour och color.', 27, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('7b121d65-3895-542d-a1c8-b237a3124dcf', 'en-ak7-brittiskt-amerikanskt-2', 'Engelska', 'ak7', 'Brittisk och amerikansk engelska', 'An email from Boston', 'Ett mejl från en flicka som har flyttat från London till Boston, med frågor om orden, våningarna och datumet som skiljer länderna åt.', 28, 'vanlig', 'Hi Olivia,

We have lived in Boston for three weeks now, and I still feel like a tourist. Everybody speaks English, of course, but it isn’t always the English we learnt in London!

On my first day at school, a girl in my class told me that she liked my pants. I went as red as a tomato, because in London pants are something you wear under your trousers! Here, the word pants just means trousers.

Our new home is an apartment, not a flat, and we live on the third floor. In London, that would be the second floor, because here the ground floor is called the first floor. The first time I took the elevator, I got out on the wrong floor.

There are other differences too. People stand in line instead of queuing, and my little brother Sam now says “cookie” instead of “biscuit”. At school we have math, not maths, and when my class sang the alphabet, everybody said “zee” at the end. I said “zed”, and the whole class laughed – in a nice way.

The funniest thing was the date on my first test. I wrote 4/10, and my teacher thought I meant the tenth of April. Here they write the month first!

Mum says we will soon speak like real Americans. I hope not – I want to keep a little bit of London.

Write soon and tell me everything!

Elsa', 'vag'),
