  ('811cfaac-3b82-520b-bd5d-0ce4023fac0a', 'en-ak9-blad-skriva-1', 'Engelska', 'ak9', 'NP-träning: skriva', 'Plan your text', 'Planera en sammanhängande text: inledning, stycken, bindeord och avslutning. Bygger på övningsbladet «NP-träning: skriva på engelska» i materialbanken.', 18, 'vanlig', null, 'np'),
  ('5ed90b35-216c-5c0b-93c1-9ec6517b8fff', 'en-ak9-blad-skriva-2', 'Engelska', 'ak9', 'NP-träning: skriva', 'Common mistakes', 'Struktur, bindeord, tempus och vanliga fel i en engelsk text. Bygger på övningsbladet «Genomgång: skriva en bra text på engelska» i materialbanken.', 19, 'vanlig', null, 'np'),
  ('ce8d548f-4b67-5efc-baeb-db6f26534717', 'en-ak9-mastare-np-traning-skriva', 'Engelska', 'ak9', 'NP-träning: skriva', 'Mästarprov: NP-träning: skriva', 'Blandade frågor ur hela området, i ny ordning varje gång. Klarar du det med minst två stjärnor sitter området.', 20, 'mastare', null, 'np'),
  ('562a1ae2-fe9a-53a4-b6ef-f3cc6c6fccc8', 'en-ak9-blad-library-1', 'Engelska', 'ak9', 'Läsa: NP-träning', 'The Library of Things', 'Läsförståelse: en artikel om att låna saker i stället för att köpa dem. Bygger på övningsbladet «NP-träning: läsa på engelska» i materialbanken.', 21, 'vanlig', 'The Library of Things

When Maya Patel needed a drill to put up a shelf, she didn''t buy one. She borrowed one from her local Library of Things, a small shop in her neighbourhood where people borrow objects instead of books.

"A drill spends most of its life in a drawer," says Tom, one of the volunteers. "It makes more sense to share it." The library lends everything from tents and sewing machines to board games and party speakers. Members pay a small fee each time they borrow something.

The idea has spread to many cities in Europe. Supporters say it saves money, reduces waste and helps neighbours get to know each other. However, not everyone is convinced. Some shop owners worry that they will sell less, and some members admit that it can be annoying when the thing you want has already been borrowed.', 'np'),
  ('9cc97e5a-8e86-544d-8632-74f7d33dbe47', 'en-ak9-blad-match-1', 'Engelska', 'ak9', 'Läsa: NP-träning', 'The Last Match', 'Läsförståelse: en kort berättelse om en fotbollsmatch, om personer och budskap. Bygger på övningsbladet «NP-träning: en kort berättelse på engelska» i materialbanken.', 22, 'vanlig', 'The Last Match

For three years, Leo had played every Saturday for the Riverside Rovers. He was not the best player on the team, but he never missed a training session, even in the rain. So when his family announced that they were moving to another city in June, the last match of the season suddenly felt like the most important game in the world.

The score was 1–1 with five minutes left. The ball bounced towards Leo near the penalty area. He could have shot, but out of the corner of his eye he saw his best friend Amir, completely unmarked. Leo passed. Amir scored.

After the final whistle, the team lifted Amir onto their shoulders. Leo stood a little to the side, smiling. Then the coach walked over and handed him the captain''s armband. "You played for the team," she said. "That''s what a captain does. Take this with you."', 'np'),
  ('3bb670bd-4de6-5a68-8fe2-b5d99421d5f6', 'en-ak9-blad-forum-1', 'Engelska', 'ak9', 'Läsa: NP-träning', 'Are zoos a good idea?', 'Läsförståelse: tre forumsinlägg om djurparker, med fakta och åsikter. Bygger på övningsbladet «NP-träning: åsikter i ett forum på engelska» i materialbanken.', 23, 'vanlig', 'Forum: Are zoos a good idea?

Maya: Zoos help endangered animals. Some species have been saved from extinction thanks to breeding programmes in zoos. I think that is amazing.

Ben: I visited a zoo last summer, and the lion just walked back and forth in a small area all day. Animals belong in the wild, not behind glass.

Priya: You both have a point. Good zoos give animals a lot of space and teach visitors about nature. Bad zoos should be closed. The problem is not zoos, it is bad zoos.', 'np'),
  ('a9643ed6-1752-59e9-b84f-b5726a9d4a4c', 'en-ak9-fler-referat-1', 'Engelska', 'ak9', 'Indirekt anföring', 'Said that, told me', 'Att återge vad någon sagt: said that, told me och tidsförskjutning.', 24, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('d0ee322a-13c5-5ff9-bde5-ba168536cbbb', 'en-ak9-fler-referat-2', 'Engelska', 'ak9', 'Indirekt anföring', 'Asked if, told to', 'Att återge frågor och uppmaningar: asked if, asked where och told me to.', 25, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('3e31819c-09f2-5626-a8ef-730e5381ffa6', 'en-ak9-mastare-indirekt-anforing', 'Engelska', 'ak9', 'Indirekt anföring', 'Mästarprov: Indirekt anföring', 'Blandade frågor ur hela området, i ny ordning varje gång. Klarar du det med minst två stjärnor sitter området.', 26, 'mastare', null, 'vag'),
  ('c0730373-664c-5e0c-89a2-c1f2d5be3923', 'en-ak9-fler-lasa-1', 'Engelska', 'ak9', 'Läsa och förstå', 'The first day at the café', 'En berättelse om första dagen på ett jobb på ett café, med frågor om vad som står och vad det betyder.', 27, 'vanlig', 'On my first day at the Blue Door Café, I dropped a tray with six cups of hot chocolate. The crash was so loud that every customer turned round, and I wanted the floor to open up and swallow me.

“Don’t worry,” said Rosa, the manager, handing me a cloth. “Everybody does it once. I did it on my second day, and the customer was wearing a white jacket.”

I had expected her to be angry. Instead she showed me how to carry a tray with the heaviest cups in the middle, and she told me to stop saying sorry to every customer. “You don’t have to say sorry for being here,” she said. “Just smile and carry on.”

By the end of the week I could carry three plates in one hand. By the end of the month I had become friends with Mr Kowal, an old man who came every morning for a black coffee and always left a coin under his saucer “for the tray girl”.

I still think about that first day. Not because I was embarrassed, but because of what Rosa said: that mistakes are only expensive if you hide them.', 'vag'),
  ('a6e8b019-54af-567b-87f3-0827dec2ab7d', 'en-ak9-fler-lasa-2', 'Engelska', 'ak9', 'Läsa och förstå', 'Teenagers and jobs', 'En text där två tonåringar och en lärare säger sitt om att ha ett extrajobb, med frågor om vad som står och vad det betyder.', 28, 'vanlig', 'Should teenagers have part-time jobs?

Mina, 15, works at a bakery every Saturday. “I earn my own money, and I have learnt to be on time,” she says. “At first I was tired on Mondays, but now I plan my weekends better. My boss says I am one of the most reliable people she has employed.”

Jack, 15, does not have a job, and he does not want one. “School is already a full-time job,” he says. “I have football training three evenings a week and homework on top of that. If I had a job as well, I would have no time to rest. There will be plenty of time to work later.”

Teachers see both sides. “A small job can teach responsibility,” says one, “but it should never get in the way of sleep or schoolwork. The key is balance.”

In the end, there is probably no single answer that is right for everyone.', 'vag'),
