  ('461f527b-08b1-5f8f-952e-0867cc09309e', 'en-gy1-stil-1', 'Engelska', 'gy1', 'Stil och idiom', 'Formell engelska', 'Formell engelska i brev, mejl och ansökningar.', 10, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('c516b262-5194-5881-ad65-e7b5731f673f', 'en-gy1-stil-2', 'Engelska', 'gy1', 'Stil och idiom', 'Idiom i sammanhang', 'Idiom som används i tal och text, och vad de betyder.', 11, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('2a1bf450-3e15-5384-b146-d58e69584fcf', 'en-gy1-mastare-stil-och-idiom', 'Engelska', 'gy1', 'Stil och idiom', 'Mästarprov: Stil och idiom', 'Blandade frågor ur hela området, i ny ordning varje gång. Klarar du det med minst två stjärnor sitter området.', 12, 'mastare', null, 'vag'),
  ('470a4381-c54a-5664-9b37-67d3ac896f45', 'en-gy1-lasforstaelse-1', 'Engelska', 'gy1', 'Läsförståelse', 'The four-day week', 'En artikel om ett företag som provar fyra dagars arbetsvecka, med frågor om fakta, ordförråd och vad personerna menar.', 13, 'vanlig', 'When the owner of Hallberg Design, a small company with twenty employees, announced that everyone would work four days a week for the same salary, most of her staff assumed it was a joke. It was not. For six months, the office would be closed on Fridays, and the company would measure what happened.

The idea was not new. Karin Hallberg had read about similar trials and was sceptical at first. “I expected that we would simply do less,” she admits. “My plan was to try it, prove it didn’t work, and move on.”

The results surprised her. The number of projects the company completed stayed roughly the same, and customers did not complain. Sick days fell by almost half. Meetings became shorter, because, as one designer put it, “when you only have four days, you stop inviting people to meetings they don’t need to be at.”

Not everyone was enthusiastic. Two employees said that the four days had become more stressful, and one of them chose to return to a five-day week with fewer hours per day. The receptionist pointed out that customers still phoned on Fridays, and a system had to be set up to answer urgent calls.

After six months, the staff voted. Eighteen out of twenty wanted to continue. Karin Hallberg decided to keep the four-day week, but with one condition: the trial would be evaluated again every year. “It works for us,” she says. “I’m not claiming it works for every company. A hospital cannot close on Fridays.”', 'vag'),
  ('6f02809f-6b35-5cb6-8644-98baa29aeb25', 'en-gy1-lasforstaelse-2', 'Engelska', 'gy1', 'Läsförståelse', 'The umbrella shop', 'En novell om en paraplyaffär som ska stänga, med frågor om vad som står, bilder i språket och vad man kan förstå mellan raderna.', 14, 'vanlig', 'Mr Okafor had sold umbrellas on Dean Street for forty-one years, and in all that time he had never once been caught in the rain without one.

The shop was narrow, dark and smelled of wood polish. Umbrellas hung from the ceiling like sleeping bats: black ones for businessmen, bright ones for tourists, and, behind the counter, a single umbrella with a carved silver handle that was not for sale.

On the last day before the shop closed for good, a girl of about ten came in, dripping. She put a pile of coins on the counter and asked for the cheapest umbrella he had.

Mr Okafor counted the coins twice. They would not have bought the handle of the cheapest one.

“That’s exactly right,” he said, and gave her a red umbrella with a wooden handle.

She looked at the silver one behind him. “Why isn’t that one for sale?”

“It belonged to my wife,” he said. “She thought umbrellas were optimistic. You only buy one if you believe you’ll still be around when it rains.”

The girl considered this seriously. Then she asked, “Are you still around?”

He laughed for the first time in weeks. “It seems I am.”

When she had gone, he looked at the empty shelves, the boxes by the door, the sign that said CLOSING DOWN. Then he took the silver umbrella from its hook, and, although the sun had come out, he opened it and walked home underneath it.', 'vag'),
  ('6b41d7b9-7ca9-50f9-879a-ca355acc3845', 'en-gy1-blad-email-1', 'Engelska', 'gy1', 'Skriva: stil och struktur', 'A formal email', 'Formella mejl på engelska: hälsning och avslutning, artiga fraser och hela former. Bygger på övningsbladet «Writing a formal email» i materialbanken.', 15, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('de9ec448-ac25-5be9-8b67-7f3b389c1cbc', 'en-gy1-blad-volunteer-1', 'Engelska', 'gy1', 'Skriva: stil och struktur', 'Should young people volunteer?', 'En argumenterande text: inledning med åsikt, topic sentences, en annan synvinkel och avslutning. Bygger på övningsbladet «NP-träning: writing, engelska nivå 1» i materialbanken.', 16, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('559574cf-30a6-5b79-b761-0fb2f9284a13', 'en-gy1-blad-formal-1', 'Engelska', 'gy1', 'Skriva: stil och struktur', 'Formal and informal', 'Formell och informell stil, stycken, bindeord och vanliga fel. Bygger på övningsbladet «Genomgång: writing, engelska 1» i materialbanken.', 17, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('f999c447-603a-5bcb-815b-dc4c2680e443', 'en-gy1-mastare-skriva-stil-och-struktur', 'Engelska', 'gy1', 'Skriva: stil och struktur', 'Mästarprov: Skriva: stil och struktur', 'Blandade frågor ur hela området, i ny ordning varje gång. Klarar du det med minst två stjärnor sitter området.', 18, 'mastare', null, 'vag'),
  ('0cab7b14-07ea-5575-85a1-6b2a39add103', 'en-gy1-blad-birds-1', 'Engelska', 'gy1', 'Läsa: NP-träning', 'Science in your back garden', 'Läsförståelse: en artikel om medborgarforskning, med huvudtanke, detaljer och attityd. Bygger på övningsbladet «NP-träning: reading, engelska nivå 1» i materialbanken.', 19, 'vanlig', 'Science in your back garden

Every winter, hundreds of thousands of people across the UK spend one hour looking out of their windows. They are not bored; they are doing science. The Big Garden Birdwatch, organised by the bird charity RSPB since 1979, asks the public to count the birds they see in their gardens or local parks and report the numbers online.

Projects like this are called citizen science: ordinary people collect data that researchers could never gather on their own. Over the years, the counts have shown worrying trends. House sparrows and starlings, for example, are far less common than they were when the counts began.

Critics point out that volunteers make mistakes. A beginner might confuse two similar species, and people who enjoy birds may be more likely to take part when their gardens are full of them. Scientists deal with this by collecting huge amounts of data and by checking unusual reports. Many participants say that once you start noticing the birds, you never really stop.', 'np'),
  ('8b12bfe7-9bd2-5fb0-be77-94dcff3fae11', 'en-gy1-blad-interview-1', 'Engelska', 'gy1', 'Läsa: NP-träning', 'The Interview', 'Läsförståelse: en kort berättelse om en anställningsintervju, med personer, detaljer och tema. Bygger på övningsbladet «NP-träning: short story, engelska 1» i materialbanken.', 20, 'vanlig', 'The Interview

Hannah had practised her answers in the mirror for a week. "Why do you want this job?" she had asked her reflection, and her reflection had answered with a confident smile. Now, sitting in the narrow corridor outside the manager''s office, she could not remember a single word.

The boy next to her was tapping his foot. He wore a suit that was clearly borrowed from someone taller. When their eyes met, he grinned. "First interview?" he whispered. She nodded. "Me too. My mum says to imagine they''re wearing pyjamas."

Hannah laughed so loudly that the receptionist looked up, and the knot in her stomach loosened. When her name was called, she stood up, smoothed her jacket and pictured the manager in striped pyjamas.

She did not get the job. But three weeks later, at a bus stop, she recognised the boy in the borrowed suit. This time she said hello first.', 'np'),
  ('5af6b6fd-ec79-5233-8237-d4bb15fd6838', 'en-gy1-fler-modals-1', 'Engelska', 'gy1', 'Modala verb och återgivet tal', 'Must have, should have', 'Tränar modala verb om det förflutna: must have, can’t have, might have och should have.', 21, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('c7fcca76-f18c-5cd5-bfb5-e398eeefce36', 'en-gy1-fler-modals-2', 'Engelska', 'gy1', 'Modala verb och återgivet tal', 'Promised to, suggested going', 'Tränar återgivet tal på högre nivå: tidsförskjutning och verb som promise, warn, suggest, admit och deny.', 22, 'vanlig', null, 'vag'),
  ('d4535194-e820-5381-ba1c-5f57308ba2e0', 'en-gy1-mastare-modala-verb-och-atergivet-tal', 'Engelska', 'gy1', 'Modala verb och återgivet tal', 'Mästarprov: Modala verb och återgivet tal', 'Blandade frågor ur hela området, i ny ordning varje gång. Klarar du det med minst två stjärnor sitter området.', 23, 'mastare', null, 'vag'),
  ('7f4943ef-0aa1-5556-9b83-a030bc71f1e2', 'en-gy1-fler-nyhet-1', 'Engelska', 'gy1', 'Läsa en nyhet', 'Pool to open late', 'En kort nyhetsartikel om en kampanj, med frågor om huvudbudskap, detaljer, ord och slutsatser.', 24, 'vanlig', 'Pool to open late after teenagers’ campaign

The town of Eastfield will keep its swimming pool open until ten o’clock on Friday evenings, after a group of teenagers collected more than 800 signatures. Until now the pool has closed at six, which many young people say is too early for anyone who has school or training during the day.

The campaign was started by sixteen-year-old Amira Haddad. “Friday evening is when my friends and I want to be together,” she said. “We used to go to the shopping centre, but there is nothing to do there if you do not want to buy anything.”

The council first said no, because late opening would cost about £12,000 a year. After meeting the teenagers, however, it agreed to try the idea for six months. A spokesperson said that the pool will only stay open late if enough people come. “If fewer than forty visitors turn up on an average Friday, we will have to think again,” she said.

The first late opening will take place on 3 November.', 'vag'),
